<title>PHILIPPINES: India gets $100 million power loan from ADB.</title>
<headline>India gets $100 million power loan from ADB.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Friday it has approved a $100 million loan to India for a project to develop renewable energy sources to help ease power shortages.</p>
<p>The project, costing $133 million, is designed to generate 125 megawatts of power.</p>
<p>The loan will carry an interest rate of 6.82 percent in accordance with the bank's variable lending rate for U.S. dollar loans. It will be payable over 25 years, including a grace period of five years, the Manila-based ADB said.</p>
</text>
